```c
/*
 * Tree files support.
 *
 * A treefiles export stores its data in a tree of small fixed-size block
 * files rather than in one large file. The exportname of such an export
 * is a directory; below it, TREEDIRSIZE (1024) entries are placed per
 * directory level, each block file holding TREEPAGESIZE (4096) bytes of
 * data. Depending on the size of the export, several levels of
 * subdirectories (named TREEXXXX) are nested below the export directory,
 * with the block files (named FILEXXXX) at the leaves.
 *
 * Block files and directories are created on demand when data is written
 * to them, and block files are removed again when the corresponding block
 * is trimmed. Blocks without a block file read back as all zeroes.
 */
```

